HR Round Interview Questions for 10 Years of Experience — Java Full Stack Developer
For a candidate with around 10 years of experience, HR discussions are not limited to basic questions like “Tell me about yourself.” Recruiters usually evaluate your communication, current and expected CTC, notice period, reason for switching, project experience, stability, location flexibility, and joining availability.
I’ve organized the questions according to the complete job-switch journey: from applying for a job to receiving and negotiating an offer. The examples are tailored to an experienced Java Full Stack Developer in the Indian IT market.
